# Written to ~/.ssh/config.local by `chezmoi apply` the first time it runs,
# then never touched again — fill in per-machine hosts here. ssh/config
# Includes this automatically, before its own Host blocks, so anything set
# here wins over the tracked config. Mode 0600 already, from the source
# name's `private_` attribute — ssh silently ignores config files that are
# group/world-readable/writable.

# A remote dev box reached by short name. The tracked ssh/config carries no
# hostnames of its own, so every machine-specific alias belongs here.
# Host devbox
#   User you

# Throwaway localhost port-forward for testing terminal tooling over ssh instead of
# a real network host. StrictHostKeyChecking/UserKnownHostsFile/LogLevel below
# turn off host-key verification entirely — safe only because the "host" is a
# local process that gets torn down and rebuilt (a new key every time would
# otherwise fail the known_hosts check). Never point these three settings at
# a real remote host.
# Host sshd-test
#   HostName localhost
#   Port 2222
#   User bash
#   IdentityFile ~/.ssh/sshd_test_ed25519
#   IdentitiesOnly yes
#   StrictHostKeyChecking no
#   UserKnownHostsFile /dev/null
#   LogLevel ERROR
